WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.357
A window calculation usually has a few pieces that answer different questions.

00:00:06.357 --> 00:00:08.667
First, what calculation do we want?

00:00:08.667 --> 00:00:12.987
Maybe an average, a rank, or a previous value.

00:00:12.987 --> 00:00:17.147
Second, should the rows be separated into groups?

00:00:17.147 --> 00:00:20.697
The partition by part defines those groups.

00:00:20.697 --> 00:00:24.577
Third, what is the sequence inside each group?

00:00:24.577 --> 00:00:27.962
The order by part defines that sequence.

00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:30.077
And for some calculations, we also define a frame.

00:00:30.077 --> 00:00:37.292
The frame says which nearby rows are included for the current row.

00:00:37.292 --> 00:00:44.282
When a window query looks complicated, separate these questions instead of trying to read everything at once.
